---
const faqs = [
  {
    q: 'Does this require any hardware — Oura Ring, wearable, anything?',
    a: 'No. Amplifly is a pure software app. You check in by tapping one of five brain states each morning. No sensors, no wearables, no external services required.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I need an account? Does it work offline?',
    a: 'Amplifly needs an account — there is no guest mode. But all your data lives on your device in local storage and every algorithm runs there, so once you\'re signed in you can use every feature — brain check-ins, conditions, flow logging, the Focus timer, the recommender, the manual — without a network connection. An account is required; a live connection is not.',
  },
  {
    q: 'How does the recommendation engine actually work?',
    a: 'It\'s a Thompson-sampling contextual bandit. Each condition is an "arm" keyed by your ND profile, brain state, and time of day. The bandit starts from research-cited priors for your profile and updates a Beta posterior every time you give feedback — thumbs up/down, or a high-intensity flow session logged within 2 hours. All computation runs on your device.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Do I have to remember to log sessions?',
    a: 'Only if you want to. The Focus tab is a built-in work timer — pick 25, 50, or 90 minutes (or no limit), turn on breaks if you want them, and hit start. When you stop, it hands you the log already filled in with the measured time. Same data, no separate step. You can also log by hand on the Flow tab, and back-date a session so a late log still lands in the right time bucket.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can I add my own techniques?',
    a: 'Yes. If you already know something works for you, add it as your own tool — name it, pick the phase it fits, and tag the brain states it helps. It shows up alongside the twelve built-ins and becomes a first-class option the recommender learns about, exactly like the built-ins. You can also record self-insights ("X helps when I\'m Y"), which feed the recommender\'s priors directly.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What neurodivergent profiles does it support?',
    a: 'ADHD, Autism, AuDHD, Dyslexia, Dyscalculia, Dyspraxia/DCD, Tourette\'s, Sensory Processing, OCD, Anxiety, Depression, PTSD/C-PTSD, Bipolar, Twice Exceptional (2e), and Other. You can select multiple — the recommender handles them as a combined profile.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What is the flow forecast?',
    a: 'A small neural network trained on synthetic data built from published research on focus and neurodivergence. The weights are fixed. A personal calibration layer blends those predictions with your own logged session data as you build history.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Is my data private?',
    a: 'Yes. Everything is stored on your device and all computation happens there. Your data also syncs to your account — encrypted in transit and stored on Supabase\'s servers solely so it\'s there on your next device. It is never sold, shared, or used for advertising, and we collect no analytics or crash reports. You can delete your account and everything in it by emailing us.',
  },
  {
    q: 'What platforms is it on?',
    a: 'Amplifly is out now on iOS — download it from the App Store. It\'s built in React Native with Expo, so an Android release is on the way; join the email list to be notified when it lands.',
  },
  {
    q: 'Can Amplifly replace therapy or medical support?',
    a: 'No. Amplifly is a self-understanding and focus tool, not a clinical product. If you need mental health support, please work with a qualified professional.',
  },
];
---
<section id="faq" class="bg-soft-blue py-24">
  <div class="container px-6 mx-auto max-w-3xl">

    <div class="text-center mb-16">
      <p class="text-bright-blue text-sm font-semibold tracking-widest uppercase mb-4">Questions</p>
      <h2 class="text-deep-navy text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold">Frequently asked</h2>
    </div>

    <div class="space-y-3">
      {faqs.map((faq, i) => (
        <div class="bg-white rounded-2xl overflow-hidden">
          <button
            class="faq-btn w-full text-left px-6 py-5 flex items-center justify-between gap-4"
            data-index={i}
            aria-expanded="false"
          >
            <span class="text-deep-navy font-semibold text-base">{faq.q}</span>
            <span class="faq-icon text-bright-blue flex-shrink-0 transition-transform duration-200 text-xl">+</span>
          </button>
          <div class="faq-answer hidden px-6 pb-5">
            <p class="text-accessible-gray text-base leading-relaxed">{faq.a}</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      ))}
    </div>

    <p class="text-center text-accessible-gray mt-10 text-sm">
      More questions? Email us at{' '}
      <a href="mailto:hello@amplifly.me" class="text-bright-blue hover:underline">hello@amplifly.me</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</section>

<script>
  document.querySelectorAll('.faq-btn').forEach(btn => {
    btn.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const answer = btn.nextElementSibling as HTMLElement;
      const icon   = btn.querySelector('.faq-icon') as HTMLElement;
      const open   = !answer.classList.contains('hidden');
      answer.classList.toggle('hidden', open);
      icon.textContent   = open ? '+' : '−';
      btn.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!open));
    });
  });
</script>
